! mcp_bootstrap_p232.strap -- MCP printed page 232: the Input Program's
! tape-switching section (V MTTSA .. V BYPAF), lines 1-56.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.239, read at 400 dpi, 900 dpi for
! doubtful glyphs.  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP
! CARD ID CA000848  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 232"; the heading
! row's LOCATION field is 225060, line 1's word.
!
! JOINS: scratch p.231 ends at 225060.00, scratch p.233 opens at
! 225120.00 -- contiguous on both sides.
!
! THE PAGE.  56 lines, every one located, contiguous from 225060.40 to
! 225117.40 (a half word; next word 225120.00).  Remarks are decimal
! sequence numbers -0830 .. -0866, printed on most rows.
!
! >>> FIVE NAMES SETTLED BY THE MANUAL, NOT THE INK (O worn to C). <<<
! docs/ocr/C22-6728*_MCP_Sys_Analysis_Guide.txt lists VOVBY, VNOP, VOPB,
! ZCOM90 and ZASN01, and no VCVBY, VNCP, VCPB or ZCON90:
!   * line 25 prints the LABEL "V CVBY"; line 16 prints B,V OVBY, whose
!     binary 225076.50 is line 25's own 225076.40.  One symbol, VOVBY.
!   * line 7 prints "V NCP"; VNOP is landed at 224157.40 and the binary
!     224157.71 is that address.  Written VNOP.
!   * line 9 prints "V CPB"; the manual's TS table gives "VOPB Flag Bit
!     .25", and 225201.31 is VSURT's word with bit 25.  Written VOPB.
!   * line 53 prints "ZCOM90" with a worn M; line 54 "ZASN?1", a round
!     the drum does not settle.  ZASN01 with a ZERO: C22-6728 PDF p.107
!     at 900 dpi sets "ZASN01 and ZDSN01" with the narrow oval of
!     "ZCOM01"'s 0, not the round of its O (its OCR reads ZASNO1).
!
! LENGTH FROM THE FINAL SYMBOL.  These statements write no dds and print
! the length of the LAST symbol in the address: "The data description of
! the final symbol ... applies to the whole combination" (C22-6531
! printed p.11).  V OPB, V RDY and V OP are SYN(BU,1), as their defining
! cards print (OCR of pp.231/234/236, not landed); V OPB = .25 and
! V RDY = .26 are bit addresses, unchanged by the point in front of them
! (C22-6578 printed p.64).
!
! LENGTH 32 FROM AN INSTRUCTION'S NAME.  L/ST with no dds print 040000.20
! when the operand names a half-word instruction: "instruction-naming
! symbols are given field lengths equal to the lengths of the particular
! instructions named (either 32 or 64) ... byte size 8" (C22-6531
! printed p.10), so those stand-in SYNs carry (BU,32,8).
!
! VDS = 3.32 and VOP = 3. are the manual's TS table (C22-6728-1: "VOP 3.
! Bit specifies REW or UNLD", "VDS 3.32 Program destination of tape");
! the binaries of lines 3 and 33 agree.
!
! Hex bytes printed with an open round, written 0 by assembly: line 5
! "C0", 9 "FC" (CM with no offset index; p.197 line 10 prints the same
! second half word "001000.36 F0"), 13 "C0", 17/29 "C1", 28 "DC", 35 and
! 56 "C1".  Octal-field opens ("CCCCC0.CC") are 0.
!
! >>> CARD SERIALS. <<<  Right-hand serials run ?A000848 .. ?A000891
! (prefix glyph as p.221's, DA/CA unsettled).  Pairs share a serial,
! the second statement's remark (if any) printed displaced to the left:
! 4/5 (851, -0833), 12/13 (858), 15/16 (860), 36/37 (880), 38/39 (881),
! 40/41 (882), 42/43 (883, -0862), 44/45 (884, -0863), 46/47 (885),
! 48/49 (886); and 53/54/55 all print 890.  Line 11 (857) prints the
! remark "-018" in the displaced column.  Remark numbers -0839, -0841,
! -0856, -0861 print nowhere.  Lines 11, 36-39, 46-49 and 56 are punched
! without the space after V ("VT5", "VS2"): written as the same symbols.
! Asterisks after the LOCATION on lines 8, 26, 47.  Line 55's VF value
! prints two columns left, as VF rows do (p.197 line 26).

VU      SYN, $3                      ! p.213 line 25 "V U SYN,$3"
VP      SYN, $1                      ! p.213 line 26 "V P SYN,$1"
VT1     SYN, $4                      ! p.213 line 27
VT2     SYN, $6                      ! p.213 line 29
VT5     SYN, $9                      ! p.213 line 28
VS2     SYN, $11                     ! p.213 line 33
VRQB    SYN, 6.32                    ! p.213 line 19 VSU.VH = 6.32
VNX     SYN, (8)5.0                  ! p.213 line 16 prints 000005.00
VTSA    SYN, (8)225210.0             ! LVI lines 1/56, half word only
VTSB    SYN, (8)225221.0             ! LVI line 8, half word only
VST     SYN, (8)225312.0             ! LVI line 2, half word only
VDS     SYN, 3.32                    ! p.234 OCR "V DS SYN,3.32" (not landed); manual "VDS 3.32"; SV line 3 half word
VOP     SYN(BU,1), 3.                ! p.234/p.236 print V OP SYN(BU,1),3. (OCR; not landed)
VSETX   SYN, (8)224671.40            ! B line 5, half word only
VNOP    SYN, (8)224157.40            ! landed; line 7 prints "V NCP"
VSURT   SYN, (8)225201.0             ! LX line 10, word only
VOPB    SYN(BU,1), .25               ! p.234 line 46 prints V OPB SYN(BU,1),.25 (OCR; not landed)
VTMV    SYN, (8)224745.40            ! B line 13, half word only
VSC1A   SYN(BU,32,8), (8)224266.0    ! label of a half-word instruction (p.217/p.228): (BU,32,8), C22-6531 printed p.10
VSQ1    SYN, (8)224322.0             ! landed p.218
VTX     SYN, (8)225246.0             ! SWAPI line 19, word only
VTXT    SYN, (8)225243.0             ! SWAPI line 19 second half, word only
VSTQ    SYN, (8)224425.40            ! landed p.221
VINOFF  SYN(BU,32,8), (8)224717.40   ! label of a half-word instruction (p.217/p.228): (BU,32,8), C22-6531 printed p.10
VSC     SYN, (8)225250.0             ! SVA line 22, LVI line 50, half word only
VSC5    SYN(BU,32,8), (8)224263.40   ! label of a half-word instruction (p.217/p.228): (BU,32,8), C22-6531 printed p.10
VIN2    SYN(BU,32,8), (8)224721.0    ! label of a half-word instruction (p.217/p.228): (BU,32,8), C22-6531 printed p.10
VOFFON  SYN, (8)224150.40            ! landed p.215
VDISP   SYN, (8)224150.0             ! landed p.215
VQ      SYN, (8)225346.0             ! LVI line 29, half word only
VRQEXT  SYN, (8)224716.40            ! SV line 30, half word only
VBREW   SYN, (8)224373.0             ! landed p.220
VWT     SYN, (8)225266.0             ! LVI line 35, half word only
VTX1    SYN, (8)225247.0             ! LX lines 36/51, word only
VCOM    SYN, (8)224702.0             ! B line 41, half word only
VACTX   SYN, (8)224653.0             ! CB+ line 43, half word only
VSCBY   SYN, (8)225127.0             ! B line 45, half word only
VSC7A   SYN, (8)224244.40            ! landed p.217
ZCOM90  SYN, (8)232762.0             ! SIC line 53, this page's binary
ZASN01  SYN, (8)232746.0             ! B line 54, half word only
VCRD    SYN, (8)5.0                  ! landed; p.100 card "- VCRD SYN,5."

        SLC, (8)225060.40
